  "worked_solution": "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\u230ax\u230b$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n\u230ax\u230b=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=1.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.5) & =\u230a-3(1.5)+1\u230b+6 \\\\  & =\u230a-4.5+1\u230b+6 \\\\  & =\u230a-3.5\u230b+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u230a-3.5\u230b=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.5) & =\u230a-3.5\u230b+6 \\\\  & =-4+6 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
